(7030769, 1066691, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Awww, poor doggie! What makes this photo is the look on that poor dog''s face and his hunched posture that speaks "I know, I was bad." Those sad, puppy dog eyes make an emotional connection - you can''t help but want to pet the poor dog. BTW nice, creative way of getting around the adding text issue.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Awww, poor doggie! What makes this photo is the look on that poor dog''s face and his hunched posture that speaks "I know, I was bad." Those sad, puppy dog eyes make an emotional connection - you can''t help but want to pet the poor dog. BTW nice, creative way of getting around the adding text issue.', '2013-05-02 02:39:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(7030771, 1065750, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Ha! O.K. you never stated it but all the visuals make a strong impression that I immediately thought it. Points for the expressive humor bit:-) Great timing on waiting for the horse to turn it''s head towards the audience. I just can''t help it....I have a critique/suggestion. I think it would have improved the visual impact more if either: you could have taken the shot when the horse was positioned more against a more solid backdrop (i.e. those green pine trees rather than the bare branches that are a tangled backdrop or failing that zoomed in closer so the horse dominates the full frame and we get more of a stare down from those eyes.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Ha! O.K. you never stated it but all the visuals make a strong impression that I immediately thought it. Points for the expressive humor bit:-) Great timing on waiting for the horse to turn it''s head towards the audience. I just can''t help it....I have a critique/suggestion. I think it would have improved the visual impact more if either: you could have taken the shot when the horse was positioned more against a more solid backdrop (i.e. those green pine trees rather than the bare branches that are a tangled backdrop or failing that zoomed in closer so the horse dominates the full frame and we get more of a stare down from those eyes.', '2013-05-02 02:48:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(7030772, 1067005, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Ah, so Sue is still around. I remember some chatter about her. Looks like she''s having a nice beach vacation:-) Lighting and scenery are good - processing on the ocean looks a bit overcooked a bit. I wonder if any other DPCer''s know or remember Sue or if this running topic/meme might be too limited to those who remember to ''get it''.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Ah, so Sue is still around. I remember some chatter about her. Looks like she''s having a nice beach vacation:-) Lighting and scenery are good - processing on the ocean looks a bit overcooked a bit. I wonder if any other DPCer''s know or remember Sue or if this running topic/meme might be too limited to those who remember to ''get it''.', '2013-05-02 02:52:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(7030773, 1066829, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment. <br/> <br/>That kitty does look like it''s trying to squeeze into/out of a tight space:-) One suggestion: I think this would have greater visual impact if the photo of the cat was more larger so we could see more of this kitty and if the sharp focus was more on the cat''s eye''s rather than the paw. The expression on the face is what carries the Meme and it''s a shame that the focus is a bit soft - it''s sharper on the chest and paw.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment.  That kitty does look like it''s trying to squeeze into/out of a tight space:-) One suggestion: I think this would have greater visual impact if the photo of the cat was more larger so we could see more of this kitty and if the sharp focus was more on the cat''s eye''s rather than the paw. The expression on the face is what carries the Meme and it''s a shame that the focus is a bit soft - it''s sharper on the chest and paw.', '2013-05-02 02:59:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(7030776, 1066965, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>I guess I''m about as lost on the strong connection to Meme as this girl is lonely on the beach. That aside - this is a lovely photo with great sunset lighting and a mood of solitary musing or loneliness depending on how you look at it. Just my thoughts but I think this would have done better in challenge more suited to playing on it''s strengths (a sunset challenge, moods, or mayhap even Free Study)</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. I guess I''m about as lost on the strong connection to Meme as this girl is lonely on the beach. That aside - this is a lovely photo with great sunset lighting and a mood of solitary musing or loneliness depending on how you look at it. Just my thoughts but I think this would have done better in challenge more suited to playing on it''s strengths (a sunset challenge, moods, or mayhap even Free Study)', '2013-05-02 03:04:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(7030777, 1066877, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Great lighting and detail on this turtle. I get the humor you are trying to convey but it needs to show it in the visuals and not rest heavily on the title explanation. With expert Editing you could have image processed in a goldfish''s tail sticking out of the turtle''s mouth. You have a solid foundation with a good photo it just needed that little extra to give it that finishing touch.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Great lighting and detail on this turtle. I get the humor you are trying to convey but it needs to show it in the visuals and not rest heavily on the title explanation. With expert Editing you could have image processed in a goldfish''s tail sticking out of the turtle''s mouth. You have a solid foundation with a good photo it just needed that little extra to give it that finishing touch.', '2013-05-02 03:08:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(7030778, 1066988, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Nice capture of a slice of daily life/street photography. I get what you are trying to convey but the photo composition needs a bit more attention to details to strongly convey it <b>within</b> the photo itself. First off, I''d recommend bringing your audience in closer to the main subject. There''s just too much negative space around her that we don''t notice the expression on her face. Get closer to your subject - show us the frustration and annoyance on her face. Expression will help make a connection with your audience. Second, show don''t tell. The impact rests too heavily on the title to identify what we should be seeing. The composition would be better if there was a sign identifying this as a bus stop or if it was taken with the woman sitting at a bus shelter. Also if you caught her looking at her watch that would more strongly convey the title.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Nice capture of a slice of daily life/street photography. I get what you are trying to convey but the photo composition needs a bit more attention to details to strongly convey it within the photo itself. First off, I''d recommend bringing your audience in closer to the main subject. There''s just too much negative space around her that we don''t notice the expression on her face. Get closer to your subject - show us the frustration and annoyance on her face. Expression will help make a connection with your audience. Second, show don''t tell. The impact rests too heavily on the title to identify what we should be seeing. The composition would be better if there was a sign identifying this as a bus stop or if it was taken with the woman sitting at a bus shelter. Also if you caught her looking at her watch that would more strongly convey the title.', '2013-05-02 03:18:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(7030782, 1066634, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>This is the third looksee at this image and there is just this creepy, eerie look to her. I guess it''s the lighting and processing that she looks a bit plastic-y or just too smooth. The expression, backdrop, and title make me think that if I get too close or disobey then this horrible monster will jump out of this girl''s skin and EAT you - sort of a monster in girl''s clothing.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. This is the third looksee at this image and there is just this creepy, eerie look to her. I guess it''s the lighting and processing that she looks a bit plastic-y or just too smooth. The expression, backdrop, and title make me think that if I get too close or disobey then this horrible monster will jump out of this girl''s skin and EAT you - sort of a monster in girl''s clothing.', '2013-05-02 03:31:41.000000', NULL, 1),
