(7030854, 1066979, 65234, '<td valign="top">Go, little dude, go!  He looks very confident in that little sports car.  The background blur doesn''t look look like motion blur to me, more like camera shake, but internet memes are often not perfect photographs.</td>', 'Go, little dude, go!  He looks very confident in that little sports car.  The background blur doesn''t look look like motion blur to me, more like camera shake, but internet memes are often not perfect photographs.', '2013-05-02 10:06:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(7030855, 1066987, 65234, '<td valign="top">Very interesting wingy things.  Would actually like to see the whole shadow, but I can see where this sort of sighting could become a meme.  Or maybe it is one already.  I don''t keep up.</td>', 'Very interesting wingy things.  Would actually like to see the whole shadow, but I can see where this sort of sighting could become a meme.  Or maybe it is one already.  I don''t keep up.', '2013-05-02 10:06:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(7030886, 1066978, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Oh wow, yeah, with those narrowed eyes that dog looks like it is about to attack. You have some great details but the lighting of the afternoon sun is just a tad harsh in highlights on the dog''s fur are blown out a bit with the shine. Yeah, I know picky, picky right:-) Understood that you sometimes just have to take the shot to get the capture but mayhap a little levels and curves can tone it down? Also I think the composition would be better if you brought us even closer to that annoyed I''m going to get you expression. Bring us closer to the action. Lastly, the border is a bit too big especially on the bottom but I think the reason for that is that you were going to add text but discovered it was not allowed (unless of course you printed it out on paper and then took a picture of it and placed it in your composition which I believe is legal).</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Oh wow, yeah, with those narrowed eyes that dog looks like it is about to attack. You have some great details but the lighting of the afternoon sun is just a tad harsh in highlights on the dog''s fur are blown out a bit with the shine. Yeah, I know picky, picky right:-) Understood that you sometimes just have to take the shot to get the capture but mayhap a little levels and curves can tone it down? Also I think the composition would be better if you brought us even closer to that annoyed I''m going to get you expression. Bring us closer to the action. Lastly, the border is a bit too big especially on the bottom but I think the reason for that is that you were going to add text but discovered it was not allowed (unless of course you printed it out on paper and then took a picture of it and placed it in your composition which I believe is legal).', '2013-05-02 11:32:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(7030889, 1066537, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Ha! Love the focus on the play on words. The tree trunk does seem to be sporting more than it should. While you had a good eye to spot this, I think there are a couple of things that could help improve the composition. First off, I think it would be better to trim off the sides so the tree then becomes the sole main focus. Also changing the compositional frame from horizontal to vertical will follow the shape of the tree and thus also compliment the shape and keep your audience focused on the main subject. Lastly, I think you could boast the dynamic tones between shadow and highlight just a bit - not too much just enough for the texture in the bark to visually pop a little more.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Ha! Love the focus on the play on words. The tree trunk does seem to be sporting more than it should. While you had a good eye to spot this, I think there are a couple of things that could help improve the composition. First off, I think it would be better to trim off the sides so the tree then becomes the sole main focus. Also changing the compositional frame from horizontal to vertical will follow the shape of the tree and thus also compliment the shape and keep your audience focused on the main subject. Lastly, I think you could boast the dynamic tones between shadow and highlight just a bit - not too much just enough for the texture in the bark to visually pop a little more.', '2013-05-02 11:39:34.000000', NULL, 1),
